    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 all tests green (AcceptanceTest is the only concrete test class in the suite).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional owner `email` field end-to-end, mirroring the existing `telephone` normalization pattern.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `email` property (string, 1\u2013255 chars) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` bind and return it.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added an `email` column, field, and getter/setter. MapStruct maps it automatically by name.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, added `owner.setEmail(normalizeEmail(owner.getEmail()))`. The new `normalizeEmail` helper:\n   - Leaves an absent/blank email unset (email is optional).\n   - Validates a present value against a syntactic email pattern; throws `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (\u2192 400) when invalid.\n   - Stores/returns the value lower-cased.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `email` column to the `owners` table, and appended `NULL` email values to the positional seed `INSERT`s in the hsqldb and mysql `data.sql` (h2/postgres already use explicit column lists).\n\n**Behavior verified by the acceptance tests:**\n- `coreLowercasesEmail` \u2014 `Test.User@Example.COM` is stored/returned as `test.user@example.com`.\n- `errorRejectsInvalidEmail` \u2014 `not-an-email` \u2192 400.\n- `functionalityAcceptsMissingEmail` \u2014 no email \u2192 2xx.",
